<!--
  Basecamp page § Outpost: the process on each box. Every claim is lifted from
  packages/outpost (README.md, CLAUDE.md, src/server.js, src/docker.js,
  src/ingress.js, src/replicate.js, src/report.js) and runs today. The proof is
  the order POST /deploy runs in, read off server.js and docker.js's swap.
  Not claimed, because it is not built: certificate expiry reported back, and
  build-once-promote-a-digest (IDEAS/deploy-plane.md).
-->
<section id="outpost" class="bc-section">
  <div class="container stack">
    <p class="eyebrow">Outpost agent</p>
    <h2>Every box runs its own apps, certificates and replicas.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Outpost is the one process Basecamp installs on each server. It does what a
      signed command asks and reports back on a timer, so the box keeps serving
      while Basecamp is down.
    </p>

    <div class="bc-split">
      <ul class="bc-points">
        <li>
          <strong>It runs your containers.</strong>
          It pulls an image by digest or builds your repository on the box, swaps the
          new container in, and puts the old one back when the release does not answer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Caddy serves HTTPS, and Outpost tells it what.</strong>
          Name a hostname and Outpost writes the app's route through Caddy's admin API,
          Caddy fetches the certificate, and the app's port moves to loopback.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your SQLite data streams off the box.</strong>
          Outpost turns Basecamp's list into the machine's Litestream config, one bucket
          key per app, and every heartbeat carries Litestream's position so a stalled
          replica shows up as lag.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Small on purpose.</strong>
          It is plain JavaScript on Bun with no schema, no ORM and no migrations,
          because its job is running Docker and reporting on volumes and disk, and it
          refuses every command Basecamp did not sign.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="bc-proof">
        <div class="flow">
          <span class="hop"><strong>Build</strong> on the box, or <strong>pull</strong> by digest</span>
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          <span class="hop"><strong>Route</strong> the hostnames in Caddy</span>
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          <span class="hop"><strong>Stop</strong> the live container, kept as <code>_replaced</code></span>
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          <span class="hop"><strong>Start</strong> the new one</span>
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          <span class="hop"><strong>Health-check</strong> for up to 30 seconds</span>
          <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          <div class="fork">
            <span class="hop"><strong>Healthy:</strong> answer the release</span>
            <span class="hop muted"><strong>Not:</strong> the old container comes back</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          What <code>POST /deploy</code> does on the box, in order:
          <code>packages/outpost/src/server.js</code> and the swap in
          <code>src/docker.js</code>. The old container is stopped first because a
          SQLite file takes one writer.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p class="bc-more">
      Read more:
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/outpost/README.md">Outpost and its protocol</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/outpost/CLAUDE.md">what bites on a box</a> ·
      <a href="https://github.com/frontierjs/frontierjs/blob/main/packages/basecamp/docs/backups.md">backups and live replicas</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* .hop, not .step: @frontierjs/css owns .step as a stepper item. */
  .flow { display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: .35rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .flow .hop { border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); border-radius: 999px; padding: .3rem .8rem; background: var(--surface-raised); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .flow .hop strong { color: var(--ink); }
  .flow .hop.muted { border-style: dashed; color: var(--ink-mute); }
  .flow .arrow { color: var(--ink-mute); padding-left: 1rem; }
  .fork { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem; }
</style>
